On Monday, Rosa will bring up to 250 millimetres of rain to some parts of Mexico.
The tropical humidity, which will then interact with the approaching low pressure, will form extensive precipitation areas in the south-west in the next few days.
Locally, precipitation of 25 to 100 millimetres causes dangerous floods of heavy rain and possibly landslides in the desert.
