Mexico's AMLO promises not to use the army against civilians
Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador, the president of Mexico, promised that he would never use military force against civilians. The announcement came as the country approached the 50th anniversary of the retaliation against students.
Lopez Obrador, who appeared in Tlatelolco Plaza on Saturday, promised that he would “never use an army to oppress the Mexican people.”
On October 2, 1968, Armed Forces fired on a peaceful demonstration, killing up to 300 people at a time when left-wing student movements were taking root in Latin America.
