The news has raised fears that sexually explicit content can be published on the accounts.
20 per centiment of pupils said they would consider a cleaned ‘main account’ for parents to be shown while using other, private accounts.
A mother finded messages written by a teenager in which she hoped she would be raped after crashing into her 13-year-old daughter's secret site.
A study commissioned by Digital Awareness UK and the Advisory Board of Directors (HMC) (HMC) found that 40 percent of young people between the ages of 11 and 18 kept two separate profiles, and half of the respondents admitted to keeping secret accounts.
HMC Director Mike Buchanan said: “It’s alarming that so many teenagers are tempted to set up online spaces where parents and teachers can’t find them.”
