The Prime Minister struggles to keep his Chequers compromise proposal afloat under pressure from Brexit supporters and opponents, as well as the EU.
The supporters demanded that he continue his attempts to reach an agreement with Brussels, notwithstanding the setback - and forcing the Eurosceptics and the Workers' Party to make a choice between his proposal and chaos.
