The flight director died to make sure that hundreds of passengers on the plane escaped an earthquake
In Indonesia, an air traffic controller has become a hero after his death to make sure that the plane carrying hundreds of passengers escaped safely into the air.
More than 800 people have died and several are missing after a powerful earthquake and a tsunami caused by it hit the island of Sulawesi on Friday.
Strong aftershocks affect the area and a number of people have been trapped among the collapsed material in the city of Palu.
